    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Harry Brann Auctioneers are delighted to bring to the market, this newly constructed 4 bedroomed detached residence built on a large elevated circa 0.37-acre site boasting panoramic views of Lough Derg & The Clare Hills. Located in a mature & much sought-after up-market development within walking distance of all amenities in the popular lakeside twin-towns of Ballina/Killaloe, the spacious property has been completed to the highest of standards and offers the would-be purchaser the ideal opportunity to put their own stamp on a modern family home -  Viewing strongly recommended.\r\n\r\nKillaloe, home of Brian Boru, the former High King of Ireland from 1002 to 1014, is situated on the banks of the River Shannon, amongst the Slieve Bernagh mountains of Clare and the Arra Hills of Tipperary at the lower end of beautiful Lough Derg. Killaloe and its twin town of Ballina are linked by an impressive 13 arch bridge which the River Shannon passes through enroute to the Atlantic Ocean."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation to include - Entrance Hall, Lounge, Open-Plan Kitchen/Dining/Living Area, Study/Home Office, 4 Bedrooms - 2 En-Suite, Family Bathroom, Utility, Shower Room & Hot-Press."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 8.05m x 1.66m \r\n+3.50m x 2.06m. Red deal stairs to first floor with rectangular window feature allowing natural light through. Understairs storage area. Recessed lighting. Telephone/computer point. \r\n\r\nLounge - 4.28m x 4.27m \r\nDual aspect windows. TV & telephone/computer points. \r\n\r\nOpen-Plan Kitchen/Dining/Living Area - \r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Area - 7.55m x 4.25m \r\nDual aspect windows to include double French doors to large patio & garden area to the rear. Recessed lighting. Ready for kitchen installation. Arched access to living area. \r\n\r\nLiving Area - 5.87m x 5.17m \r\nTreble aspect windows to include double French door access to large patio & garden area to the rear. TV & telephone/computer points. Plumbed for wood-burning stove. Recessed lighting. \r\n\r\nStudy/Home Office - 3.91m x 3.37m \r\nBay window. TV & telephone/computer points. \r\n\r\nUtility - 3.37m x 2.33m \r\nPlumbed for washing machine & dryer. Plant controls for under-floor heating. Side door access. \r\n\r\nShower Room - 3.38m x 1.51m \r\nPlumbed for large electric shower. WC & WHB. \r\n\r\nFirst-Floor Landing - 6.46m x 2.08m \r\n+2.41m x 0.61m. Recessed lighting. Stira stairs access to floored attic storage place.\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom Suite - 5.23m x 2.94m \r\nBright & spacious. Large picture-view window to include double French doors to south-facing balcony boasting panoramic views of Lough & The Clare Hills. TV & telephone/computer points. \r\n\r\nWalk-in Wardrobe - 2.63m x 1.81m \r\nIncluded Above. \r\n\r\nEn-Suite - 2.63m x 1.97m \r\n\r\n\r\nGuest Bedroom 2 - 5.17m x 4.33m \r\nPicture view window boasting panoramic views of Lough & The Clare Hills. TV & telephone/computer points. \r\n\r\nEn-Suite - 2.66m x 1.72m \r\nIncluded Above. Plumbed for large electric shower, WC & WHB. \r\n\r\nHot-Press - 1.49m x 1.26m \r\nControls for first-floor under-floor heating. Water tank.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom - 3.07m x 2.45m \r\nPlumbed for large shower, bath, WC & WHB. Recessed lighting. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 4.87m x 2.95m \r\nTV & telephone/computer points. \r\n\r\nBedroom 4 - 4.71m x 3.85m \r\nDouble French door access to rear balcony overlooking rear garden area. TV & telephone/computer points. \r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Services to include - Air to water heat pump with under-floor heating on both floors & heat recovery system. Mains water & sewerage.\r\nHollowcore concrete beams between floors. Fully painted.   \r\nPVC treble-glazed windows & doors. Front & rear balconies. \r\nNeatly landscaped lawned gardens to the front, sides & rear with picket fencing in concrete posts. Large patio area to the rear. Base laid for garden shed.\r\nIdeally located at the hub of the mid-west - University of Limerick - 27 mins, J27, M7 Motorway - 10mins & Shannon Airport - 45 mins."
      },
      {
